    "reading": "The 10.2 the flux layer records as an unexplained single-compartment residual is yeast-GEM disagreeing with itself, in kcal/mol. Most of it is the proton: matTFA prices H+ at RT ln(10) pH and then never adds it into a reaction sum, while yeast-GEM ships that number in the metabolite column, so summing the column charges it once per net proton. The rest is the compartment collapse. Neither is evidence about eQuilibrator."
